We delve into the Fenton type problems in the context of functions with multiple translations, building on the existing work of the second author's earlier research. Our investigation centers around the problem of identifying the most effective $L^p$ norm for the Fourier transform of a function with total of translations form $\left\|\sum_{k=1}^m c_k e^{ix\cdot\eta_k(x)}f(x)\right\|_{L^p(\mathbb{R}^d)}$, given a fixed $L^p$ norm for $f$. Our results encompass:

a) Derivation of the upper limit of the Fenton type problem for $1\leq p<\infty$ and arbitrary dimension $d$, with findings that align with previous research by the second author's work for $d=1$;

b) Proof of the existence of extremal functions for $1\leq p<\infty$ in the context of the Fenton type problem;

c) Investigation of the asymptotic behavior of the Fenton type problem as the number of translations increases, in the context of the $d=1$ case for $1\leq p<\infty$.

